From b0181d4cb5ded568e39b4ea711f3c644be14edf1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RubberDingyRapids <smellthellama@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 20:00:55 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] cloud: run extra Bambu accounts next to the logged-in one

The slicer only knows one account. A companion Orca plugin can now list
more in <config_dir>/obn.accounts.json (obn.auth.json's keys plus
enabled/label); the library only reads it.

- One CloudSession per enabled extra account, started with the primary
  connection and stopped with it. They share connect_cloud's report and
  subscribe-failure handlers.
- get_user_print_info appends each extra account's printers (optionally
  as "[label] name"), records dev_id -> owning account, and skips
  printers an earlier account already listed.
- Subscribe, publish, pushall kickstart, cloud print, the /user/ttcode
  camera mint, firmware lookup, rename and unbind use the owner's
  connection/token.
- Errors from an extra account's printers are not passed to
  on_http_error, so a 401 there cannot log the slicer out.
- New exports obn_extra_accounts_api / _reload / _status for the plugin.
  Reload re-reads the file, restarts the extra sessions and asks the
  slicer to refetch its device list via the user-topic bind notice,
  naming the already-selected printer so the selection is unchanged.

Without obn.accounts.json nothing changes.
